{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe hourly host updater `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh` installs a Git URL through pipx. Commit `4214516f95` made the repository uv-lock-canonical and declared the `eval`+`dev` extra combination incompatible; commit `31844d5f9f` correctly overrides Inspect AI's stale `click<8.2.2` cap and locks Click 8.4.2 to remediate PYSEC-2026-2132. The override is workspace-only and is not published in wheel metadata. The updater therefore bypasses both the committed lock and the Click override, and its 2026-08-04 01:27 run failed unlocked resolution while leaving the global host runtime stale at `d72c4777`. This blocks A2-2 and later A6-1 rollout evidence.\n\n## Approach\n- Preserve `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, the Click override, and all dependency declarations unchanged.\n- Replace the pipx VCS-resolution step with an exact-SHA, versioned local checkout under the updater state directory and `uv sync --locked`.\n- Sync the runtime/operator extras `mcp`, `reviewbot`, `ui`, `agents`, `eval`, `tracing`, `grounding`, and `grounding-t2` with `--no-dev`. Development tools are intentionally excluded from the global runtime; `eval` remains available, and the declared `eval`+`dev` conflict is respected.\n- Smoke-test the candidate checkout's `rebar` and `rebar-mcp`, verify the locked Click version, then atomically publish the host shims and checkpoint SHA. A failed candidate must leave the previous published runtime and checkpoint untouched.\n- Trigger the updater through launchd and verify an immediately following no-op.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The updater checks out the exact SHA returned by `git ls-remote` and runs `uv sync --locked` in that checkout. Tier: deterministic script-content check.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The sync requests `mcp`, `reviewbot`, `ui`, `agents`, `eval`, `tracing`, `grounding`, and `grounding-t2`, passes `--no-dev`, and does not change repository dependency metadata. Tier: deterministic script diff.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Candidate smoke or sync failure leaves the previously published executable paths and `last-good.sha` byte-identical. Tier: disposable-state failure probe.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A launchd-triggered real install exits 0 and advances `last-good.sha` to the exact `origin/main` SHA used for the run.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar` and `rebar-mcp` resolve into the versioned exact-SHA runtime.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The published runtime reports Click 8.4.2, and `pip-audit` reports no PYSEC-2026-2132 finding for that environment.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The published global build loads this repository's effective criteria and both updater smoke commands exit 0.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] An immediately following launchd run logs `no change (already on <installed-sha>)` and exits 0.\n\n## Files\nMachine-local `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/rebar-dev-update.sh` and updater-managed state under `/Users/joeoakhart/.local/state/rebar-dev/`; no repository files.\n\nScope: S. Discovered while collecting A2-2 rollout evidence.","title":"Host updater bypasses the committed uv lock and Click security override"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785808124281623001,"uuid":"f2e9fbfc-02c6-4653-b88d-e182956045c1"}